+# BLOCKED: September 2026 reconciliation
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` cannot run because the September ledger export is
+missing:
+
+```
+exports/ledger_2026-09.csv
+```
+
+`reconcile.main()` loads both `exports/ledger_<month>.csv` and
+`exports/bank_<month>.csv`. Only the bank side exists for September:
+
+```
+exports/bank_2026-09.csv
+```
+
+The command fails with:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+As a result, `recon_2026-09.json` and its net difference could not be produced.
+
+## Why this cannot be worked around
+
+The missing file is the source of the ledger side of the reconciliation. It has
+never existed in this repository (checked `exports/` and the full git history),
+and there is no alternative ledger export elsewhere in the project. Treating the
+ledger as empty, reusing `ledger_2026-08.csv`, or synthesizing September entries
+would produce an incorrect net difference and could misstate the reconciliation,
+so none of those were done.
+
+The September bank statement is present and contains four invoice lines
+(INV-9001 through INV-9004) plus two others (INV-9005, FEE-0901). Without the
+corresponding ledger export there is no way to determine matched,
+mismatched, or missing entries, or the bank-minus-ledger difference.
+
+## What was completed
+
+- Implemented `reconcile()` in `reconcile.py` (match by `ref`, classify
+  matched / amount-mismatch / missing on either side, compute net difference
+  as bank total minus ledger total with two decimals).
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile.py`: both tests pass.
+- Verified the full script end to end with the available August data:
+  `python3 reconcile.py 2026-08` produced `recon_2026-08.json`
+  (net difference `-19.59`).
+
+## To unblock
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` with columns `id,date,ref,amount`, then run:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
